dsh-security

This project integrates, but does not vendor, @openai/codex-security 0.2.0
and native Codex/SDK 0.162.0-alpha.15. Those components and their transitive
dependencies retain their upstream licenses and notices in the built image.
Published SDK source: https://github.com/openai/codex-security
Published package git SHA: 4949af70fcfadff154f6e8fdf100faa5bf2f8169

engine/seccomp.json is a MODIFIED version of Moby's Apache-2.0 seccomp
profile from commit 6fe7deb1b9fb7c0397a4593480d7d22b9ee8caef:
https://github.com/moby/profiles/blob/6fe7deb1b9fb7c0397a4593480d7d22b9ee8caef/seccomp/default.json
Modifications: require CLONE_NEWUSER for the additional clone rule;
allow namespace-only unshare flags; allow mount, umount2, pivot_root and
sethostname for unprivileged nested Bubblewrap namespaces. No outer
capabilities are added. Copyright remains with the Moby contributors.
The Apache-2.0 license is supplied in LICENSE. See engine/seccomp.README.md.

engine/models.json is an original minimal runtime catalog template with
original security-analysis instructions. It does not reproduce third-party
instruction templates. Codex model-catalog field compatibility was checked
against DeepSeek's public native Codex integration documentation:
https://api-docs.deepseek.com/quick_start/agent_integrations/codex/
At runtime its model identity/context come from the selected Harness model;
provider authentication remains with the configured Harness adapter.

Node.js, Debian packages, and installed npm dependencies are obtained
by the engine build and retain their original licenses. This repository
does not contain their binaries or downloaded source trees.
